// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-walking-pads-for-tall-people/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-14",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-14",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "best walking pad for tall people",
      "walking pad for tall person",
      "long walking pad",
      "walking pad 48 inch belt",
      "under desk treadmill for tall people",
      "walking pad 6 foot 4",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: WalkingPad Z1R", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Walking Pad for Tall People Six Long-Belt Picks</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Most walking pads have belts around 40 inches long, which is fine at an amble and cramped for a tall walker at a brisk pace. A handful run to 47 or 48 inches. Here are six of them, checked against the brands and independent sources, the rough arithmetic for how much belt you need, and the point at which a full treadmill is the better buy.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated October 14, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#walkingpad-z1r"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/419oUO9ShtL._SL500_.jpg" alt="WalkingPad Z1R" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#walkingpad-z1"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31oMu9TYTUL._SL500_.jpg" alt="WalkingPad Z1" width="448" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#lifespan-tr5000pro-glowup"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/314eClzr28L._SL500_.jpg" alt="LifeSpan TR5000Pro-GlowUp" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>WalkingPad Z1R · WalkingPad Z1 · LifeSpan TR5000Pro-GlowUp</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          If you are over about six feet tall, the best walking pad for you is the one with enough
          belt for your stride, and most pads do not have it. The typical pad's belt is around 40
          inches long, and a tall walker at a brisk pace can need nearly all of that for the space
          between one heel strike and the next, before allowing for the length of a shoe. A short
          belt does not usually throw you off; it makes you shorten your step without noticing,
          which feels cramped and changes how you walk. This page lists six pads whose belts run
          from 47 to 48 inches, explains how to estimate the length you need, and says plainly
          when a full treadmill with a longer deck is the better machine.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-z1r">WalkingPad Z1R</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Budget:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-z1">WalkingPad Z1</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Long Workdays:</span> <a href="#lifespan-tr5000pro-glowup">LifeSpan TR5000Pro-GlowUp</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Tall and Heavy:</span> <a href="#lifespan-tx6-glowup">LifeSpan TX6-GlowUp</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best With Handles:</span> <a href="#redliro-walking-treadmill">Redliro Walking Treadmill for Seniors</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best for Walking and Jogging:</span> <a href="#walkingpad-r3-hybrid-plus">WalkingPad R3 Hybrid+</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[5].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below.</strong> We have not tested these
          walking pads. Belt length was the figure we checked hardest: each pad's walking area or
          belt dimensions were checked on 14 October 2026 against the brand's own product page
